# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the minimal test suite.
#
# The headless E2E tier exercises a real multi-process shape: the spawned
# server and the test binary open the same SQLite database (WAL mode). All
# cross-process synchronization -- WAL shared-memory locks, fcntl file locks
# -- is invisible to TSan, so every race whose frames land inside sqlite's
# parser/lexer/mutex internals is noise from two sqlite3 handles sharing one
# WAL file, not a finding. First-party code's own locking (SessionDatabase's
# one-connection-one-mutex discipline) is NOT covered by this and still
# reports. called_from_lib is unusable here: it matches by name, and the
# system libsqlite3 and the vcpkg-built one are both "libsqlite3.dylib",
# which makes the runtime abort on the ambiguity.
race:sqlite3*
race:yy_*
race:keywordCode
race:pthreadMutexNotheld
